---
import PolicyLayout from "../layouts/PolicyLayout.astro";
import { SUPPORT_EMAIL, DEMO_URL, DOCS_URL, APP_URL } from "../lib/site";
const contact = "mailto:" + SUPPORT_EMAIL + "?subject=" + encodeURIComponent("BlogStack early access") + "&body=" + encodeURIComponent("Hi, I'd like to try BlogStack.\n\nWebsite:\nFramework:\nAre you publishing for yourself or a client?\n");
---
<PolicyLayout title="Try BlogStack with your next website" description="Private access for developers and agencies who want to give clients a place to publish.">
  <p>We are onboarding a small group before opening public signup. Plans and the no-card Studio trial are prepared; paid checkout is currently closed.</p>
  <h2>See the publication first</h2><p>Explore the <a href={DEMO_URL}>live blog built with BlogStack</a>, or follow the <a href={DOCS_URL + "/docs/quickstart"}>Next.js installation guide</a>. The public SDK and editable components are available now.</p>
  <h2>Request an invitation</h2><p><a href={contact}>Email {SUPPORT_EMAIL} for early access</a>. Include your website, framework and whether you are building for a client. We will reply with the next steps. Sending a request does not create an account or subscription.</p>
  <p>Already invited? Use the link in your invitation email, or <a href={APP_URL + "/login"}>sign in to your workspace</a>.</p>
</PolicyLayout>
